  "content": {
    "display_title": "The selected GNS representation of a pure-state class",
    "one_sentence_role": "A choice of representative pure states, fixed literally at a root, gives one concrete GNS representation per equivalence class.",
    "natural_language_statement": "Let $A$ be a unital complex C*-algebra, with the positive order used for its states, and fix a pure state $\\omega$. A pure state is an extreme point of the normalized positive continuous linear functionals. Let $I$ be the set of pure-state GNS representations modulo unitary equivalence. For each $j\\in I$, choose a pure state $\\varphi_j$ in that class, retaining $\\varphi_o=\\omega$ literally at $o=[\\omega]$. Write $(H_j,\\pi_j,\\xi_j)$ for its GNS space, representation and canonical cyclic vector. The selected representation is the GNS action $\\pi_j:A\\to B(H_j)$ associated to this particular $\\varphi_j$. The choice concerns the representative state; the construction then uses its actual GNS Hilbert space and action.",
    "definition_explanation": "Take the chosen state $\\varphi_j$, regard it as a positive linear functional, and form its GNS completion $H_j$. Left multiplication induces the bounded action $\\pi_j$ on that completion. The selected vector $\\xi_j$ is the GNS cyclic vector. Its orbit $\\pi_j(A)\\xi_j$ is dense. The vector-functional identity and purity of $\\varphi_j$, together with this cyclicity and normalization, supply the separate irreducibility theorem.",
    "assumptions": "The class $j\\in I$ and the root pure state $\\omega$ are given. GNS representations here are unital complex-linear star homomorphisms on complete complex Hilbert spaces. No separability or faithfulness of $\\pi_j$ is assumed.",
    "conclusion": "The definition specifies $\\pi_j$ on $H_j$. The separate selected-vector and pure-GNS results give $\\|\\xi_j\\|=1$, $\\varphi_j(a)=\\langle\\xi_j,\\pi_j(a)\\xi_j\\rangle$, and irreducibility of $\\pi_j$. These properties explain why this selected family supplies the summands of the direct-sum representation.",
    "proof_summary": null,
    "proof_steps": [],
    "lean_realization_notes": "The inner product is conjugate linear in its first argument. Irreducibility means that the only closed reducing subspaces are $0$ and $H_j$; this Hilbert space is nonzero because it contains the unit vector $\\xi_j$. The definition does not itself prove those properties, and it does not claim that different pure states always have inequivalent GNS representations.",
    "content_completeness": "CARD_CONTENT_COMPLETE",
    "language_tag": "en"
  },
